{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"exergy efficiency exergy efficiency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md","fileName":"Exergy Efficiency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Exergy Efficiency","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 22:37\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Energy Systems Appraisal]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Energy Systems Appraisal","Exergy","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"exergy efficiency exergy efficiency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md","fileName":"Exergy Efficiency.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Exergy Efficiency","heading":"Exergy Efficiency","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Exergy efficiency compares useful-product [[Exergy]] with the exergy entering a system: $\\epsilon=E_{useful}/E_{in}=1-E_{destroyed}/E_{in}$. It is a second-law performance measure because it tracks whether energy quality survives conversion, not merely whether heat or electrical energy is accounted for. A device may have respectable energy efficiency yet low exergy efficiency when it delivers heat at a temperature poorly matched to its source.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Energy Systems Appraisal","Exergy","directenergyconversiontechnologies.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"exergy efficiency exergy efficiency","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Exergy Efficiency.md","file